 · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]2[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]ci_master_red_recovery.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/ci_master_red_recovery.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-fq[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-fq/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bump the published sase-core-rs window to 0.18.1[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-window[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-window: raise the pyproject sase-core-rs constraint (and uv.lock) [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from >=0.17.15,<0.18.0 to >=0.18.1,<0.19.0 so the bead relocation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]binding sase already calls is guaranteed present.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Give progress_fingerprint an import symvision can see[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]symvision-import[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]symvision-import: make commit_finalizer.py import progress_fingerprint [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]explicitly instead of reaching it through a module alias, so the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]symvision lint stage stops reporting it as an unused public symbol.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Configure a git identity on the sidecar clone in the git-sync [bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]fixtures[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]sidecar-git-identity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sidecar-git-identity: set user.name/user.email on the sidecar clone [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]built by setup_repo so tests that commit there stop failing with exit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]128 on runners where git cannot auto-detect an identity.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop the real-uv harness leaking lock files into the watched [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]temp root[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]uv-harness-tmpdir[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]uv-harness-tmpdir: give the uv_env fixture its own TMPDIR under tmp_path[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so real uv subprocesses stop dropping uv-setuptools-*.lock into the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]managed SASE temp root and tripping the session temp-leak guard.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keep CI's prebuilt core wheel installed for every just recipe [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]in a job[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]ci-wheel-pin[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ci-wheel-pin: stop later just recipes from silently re-resolving [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core-rs back to a published wheel, so source lanes really do test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase-core commit that build-core built, and add CI-shape coverage [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that locks the behavior in.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the silent 2s commit-log budget in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-commit-budget[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-commit-budget: replace the hard, silently-empty two-second git log [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]budget in the artifact-ref commit inventory with a generous and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]overridable one, land it in sase-core, and get a release published.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the released c